00:03:59.439 --> 00:03:59.872
Lanny,

00:03:59.872 --> 00:04:00.740
what is your sense

00:04:00.740 --> 00:04:02.475
of what happens from here

00:04:02.475 --> 00:04:03.743
in these uncharted waters

00:04:03.743 --> 00:04:05.612
in terms of timing? Right.

00:04:05.612 --> 00:04:06.212
You get it

00:04:06.212 --> 00:04:07.247
and I will just say, by the way,

00:04:07.247 --> 00:04:07.780
I want everyone to know

00:04:07.780 --> 00:04:08.781
what you're seeing on your screen.

00:04:08.781 --> 00:04:10.917
Alvin Bragg, the district attorney,

00:04:10.917 --> 00:04:13.119
just departing the Manhattan

00:04:13.753 --> 00:04:15.421
Manhattan courthouse downtown.

00:04:15.421 --> 00:04:16.723
So you can see that happening.

00:04:16.723 --> 00:04:17.790
We had known where he was.

00:04:17.790 --> 00:04:18.891
We can tell you that he left.

00:04:18.891 --> 00:04:19.826
But obviously,

00:04:19.826 --> 00:04:20.593
just getting into that

00:04:20.593 --> 00:04:22.328
SUV, as you can see there,

00:04:22.328 --> 00:04:23.630
into that Chevy.

00:04:23.630 --> 00:04:25.365
Lenny, let me just ask you, though,

00:04:25.365 --> 00:04:28.268
do you have any sense as to the timing,

00:04:28.268 --> 00:04:29.402
what happens here?

00:04:29.402 --> 00:04:30.169
Right.
Right now,

00:04:30.169 --> 00:04:30.937
we're in

00:04:30.937 --> 00:04:32.138
the very first step,

00:04:32.138 --> 00:04:33.606
which is our reporting

00:04:33.606 --> 00:04:35.041
is early next week.

00:04:35.041 --> 00:04:37.143
Donald Trump will surrender. Right.

00:04:37.143 --> 00:04:38.578
We'll have the arrest. Right.

00:04:38.578 --> 00:04:39.646
And then we move from there.

00:04:39.646 --> 00:04:40.947
How does the timing go from there

00:04:40.947 --> 00:04:41.981
as far as you understand it?

00:04:43.750 --> 00:04:44.217
Well, the

00:04:44.217 --> 00:04:47.220
speedy trial process will occur, but Mr.

00:04:47.220 --> 00:04:50.023
Trump is entitled to a strong defense.

00:04:50.456 --> 00:04:52.425
I am familiar with his defense attorney.

00:04:52.425 --> 00:04:53.760
We worked together in his past.

00:04:53.760 --> 00:04:55.261
He's a very good attorney.

00:04:55.261 --> 00:04:56.929
And as I reminded your viewers,

00:04:56.929 --> 00:04:57.664
I hope not

00:04:57.664 --> 00:04:59.299
that surprising anyone

00:04:59.299 --> 00:05:01.501
that Donald Trump is presumed innocent.

00:05:01.801 --> 00:05:03.603
And while he is politicizing

00:05:03.603 --> 00:05:04.837
by calling it a witch hunt

00:05:04.837 --> 00:05:06.639
and all of the things that Trump does

00:05:06.639 --> 00:05:07.740
to deflect.

00:05:07.740 --> 00:05:09.876
I would ask everybody watching tonight,

00:05:09.876 --> 00:05:10.777
keep your minds

00:05:10.777 --> 00:05:12.645
open to the actual evidence.

00:05:12.645 --> 00:05:14.814
Documents speak for themselves.

00:05:14.814 --> 00:05:16.816
Witnesses that are more than one

00:05:16.816 --> 00:05:17.884
witness speak,

00:05:17.884 --> 00:05:19.652
and then the jury will have to decide

00:05:19.652 --> 00:05:20.687
whether they're credible.

00:05:20.687 --> 00:05:22.155
But, Erin, the most important thing

00:05:22.155 --> 00:05:22.755
I would urge

00:05:22.755 --> 00:05:24.624
all of your panelists

00:05:24.624 --> 00:05:27.360
is to at least know what they don't know

00:05:27.727 --> 00:05:29.996
and wait for the evidence that we'll see

00:05:30.396 --> 00:05:31.331
in the indictment

00:05:31.331 --> 00:05:32.665
and then, of course, in the trial

00:05:32.665 --> 00:05:34.767
that I believe will be relatively soon.

00:05:34.767 --> 00:05:35.335
And Lanny,

00:05:35.335 --> 00:05:36.135
I mean, in a sense, right

00:05:36.135 --> 00:05:36.836
now, you're being

00:05:36.836 --> 00:05:38.071
you're not being emotional about it.

00:05:38.071 --> 00:05:39.906
Obviously, your client, Michael Cohen,

00:05:39.906 --> 00:05:42.141
is is less judicious with his words.

00:05:42.141 --> 00:05:44.410
Right.
He's referred to Trump's evil deeds.

00:05:44.410 --> 00:05:45.745
Do you think that

00:05:46.779 --> 00:05:47.146
he should

00:05:47.146 --> 00:05:50.316
not do that, that that's gone too far?

00:05:50.316 --> 00:05:51.851
Well, this is the expression

00:05:51.851 --> 00:05:53.086
Michael Cohen

00:05:53.086 --> 00:05:54.520
used with me

00:05:54.520 --> 00:05:56.522
when he asked me to help him.

00:05:56.522 --> 00:05:57.256
And I said,

00:05:57.256 --> 00:05:58.291
tell me what you did

00:05:58.291 --> 00:05:59.859
for the last ten years.

00:05:59.859 --> 00:06:01.627
How can I possibly defend that

00:06:01.627 --> 00:06:02.628
when you work for Mr.

00:06:02.628 --> 00:06:03.229
Trump

00:06:03.229 --> 00:06:04.630
and all the things that I believe

00:06:04.630 --> 00:06:05.131
you did?

00:06:05.131 --> 00:06:06.733
And he used the expression,

00:06:06.733 --> 00:06:09.335
I cannot defend the evil deeds

00:06:09.335 --> 00:06:11.104
I did for Donald Trump.

00:06:11.104 --> 00:06:13.306
So on July 2nd 2018,

00:06:13.473 --> 00:06:15.641
he became a new Michael Cohen.

00:06:15.875 --> 00:06:17.877
He decided to speak truth to power

00:06:17.877 --> 00:06:19.412
and take the consequences.

00:06:19.412 --> 00:06:20.313
He went to prison

00:06:20.313 --> 00:06:22.081
for the very same crimes

00:06:22.081 --> 00:06:23.216
that the Southern District

00:06:23.216 --> 00:06:23.649
of New York

00:06:23.649 --> 00:06:24.817
Federal prosecutors

00:06:24.817 --> 00:06:27.720
described as a threat to our democracy.

00:06:27.954 --> 00:06:30.123
It's not just a hush money sex crime.

00:06:30.423 --> 00:06:31.858
It is what the Southern District

00:06:31.858 --> 00:06:34.093
prosecutors under Donald Trump said.

00:06:34.327 --> 00:06:35.128
He directed

00:06:35.128 --> 00:06:37.063
Michael Cohen to do these crimes.

00:06:37.063 --> 00:06:38.531
Those were the dirty deeds.

00:06:38.531 --> 00:06:41.033
He paid the hush money on behalf of Mr.

00:06:41.033 --> 00:06:43.202
Trump for Mr. Trump benefit.

00:06:43.436 --> 00:06:45.438
But I still want to remind everyone Mr.

00:06:45.438 --> 00:06:47.473
Trump deserved his day in court.

00:06:47.473 --> 00:06:49.575
He can demonize the opposition.

00:06:49.575 --> 00:06:51.010
But I am saying let's

00:06:51.010 --> 00:06:51.978
wait for the evidence

00:06:51.978 --> 00:06:54.046
and give him the presumption of innocence

00:06:54.046 --> 00:06:55.815
that the Constitution provides.

00:06:55.815 --> 00:06:56.449
Right. Right.

00:06:56.449 --> 00:06:57.750
And of course, to remind our viewers,

00:06:57.750 --> 00:06:59.352
hush money payments themselves are not

00:06:59.352 --> 00:07:00.420
what would be illegal here.

00:07:00.420 --> 00:07:01.821
It would be how they were accounted for

00:07:01.821 --> 00:07:03.756
and how they were handled

00:07:03.756 --> 00:07:04.924
So while this

00:07:04.924 --> 00:07:06.225
may seem salacious, it's

00:07:06.225 --> 00:07:08.561
not it's not a revenge or anything.

00:07:08.561 --> 00:07:10.029
It is about motivation.

00:07:10.029 --> 00:07:11.998
And the jury will have to decide that Mr.

00:07:11.998 --> 00:07:14.200
Trump had no political motivation

00:07:14.200 --> 00:07:15.868
about the harm that might occur

00:07:15.868 --> 00:07:16.536
to people.

00:07:16.536 --> 00:07:17.303
Chances

00:07:17.303 --> 00:07:17.970
at the Stormy

00:07:17.970 --> 00:07:20.740
Daniels alleged affair came out.

00:07:20.740 --> 00:07:22.742
And that is the issue before the jury.

00:07:22.742 --> 00:07:24.177
And I trust the jury system.

